# Settings for compose.yaml at 1M context (1,048,576 tokens), one pair on a 4x B200
# with ~880 GiB of host RAM (g1m-b200.4x):
#   docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file dsv41-1m.env up --no-deps pd
# UNQUALIFIED: no B200 run has gone past 262K context, and HiCache has not been
# booted on B200 with this recipe since 2026-10-18. Every number below is an
# estimate from the 262K and 131K measurements until the first 1M boot.
# Values run to the end of the line; no shell expansion.

# The engine image by digest: the images-<commit> release of
# confidential-sglang names it (ghcr.io/confidential-dot-ai/confidential-sglang/engine@sha256:...).
DSV41_IMAGE=
# DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 with NVIDIA's MXFP4 Engram tables (97 GiB of Engram,
# not 189), assembled by the checkpoint service (launcher/prepare_checkpoint.py
# spec 1017-mxfp4-engram, confidential-sglang PR #25; merge that first). The
# ~98 GiB of host RAM it frees goes to HiCache. FP8 Engram works too (set
# DSV41_MODEL to the plain 1017 checkpoint and clear DSV41_CHECKPOINT); auto
# still reaches the HiCache cap.
DSV41_MODEL=/data/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-mxfp4-engram
DSV41_CHECKPOINT=1017-mxfp4-engram
DSV41_DATA=/data/dsv41-bringup

# One pair: prefill on GPUs 0-1, decode on GPUs 2-3 of a 4x B200 VM.
GPUS=0,1,2,3
PORT=8040
BOOTSTRAP_PORT=8999
NCCL_PORT=29600
ROUTER_METRICS_PORT=29001

# dsv41-262k.env's flags with these changes:
# --context-length 1048576 (the model's max_position_embeddings).
# --memory-profile B200: the launch plan carries the per-rank HBM estimate below,
#   and preflight checks memory.total. Pool sizes stay explicit.
# --max-total-tokens 1572864 (prefill pool, 262K: 1048576): one full 1M prompt
#   plus 512K tokens for the other admitted prompts and the prefix cache. At
#   1048576 a 1M prompt fills the pool: every other prefill waits behind it until
#   its KV reaches decode, and its whole prefix cache is evicted to HiCache.
# --decode-max-total-tokens 6291456 (262K: 4194304): six full 1M conversations
#   resident at once, or one plus 127 of ~40K. --decode-requests stays 128: at
#   long contexts the pool, not the slot count, is the limit.
# Both roles wait up to 20 min for a KV handoff (SGLANG_DISAGGREGATION_WAITING_TIMEOUT,
#   default 5 min), as in dsv41-b200-1m.env: a 1M request queued behind another
#   cold 1M prefill can exceed 300 s before its transfer completes.
# Router admission, queue and the 30 s queue timeout as in 262K (one pair).
#   The router's request timeout stays at its 1800 s default: a 1M prompt's
#   prefill (minutes) plus its output must finish inside it.
# HiCache auto, capped at 8: 8 x the 1.5M pool = 12M host tokens, ~90 GiB for
#   the prefill worker (both ranks). build_layouts.py plans it at 768 GiB.
# Kept from 262K: 8K chunks (12K chunks OOMed prefill at 262K), the 65536 prefill
#   graph cap (past it, chunks run eagerly; a larger cap hit an illegal memory
#   access in replay, 2026-10-20), --warmups confidential_cold_path and
#   --loader-threads 2. The cold-path warmup stops at 32K-token prompts, so the
#   first long request after ready may still compile kernels.
#
# Memory per rank (GiB), from launch.py's B200 model (GPU_PROFILES and the
# 2026-10-19 TP2 measurements; launch plan "memory" section):
#   HBM 179.06 = context 3.81 + weights 146.76 (target 142.88 + DSpark draft 3.88)
#   + CUDA graphs (prefill 9.74 at 8K chunks, decode 1.75) + KV pool + free.
#   KV: 1938 B/token per rank (latent 584 B at KV sources 2/8/14 ratio 2 and 20
#   ratio 1 = 1460 B, FP4 index 68 B x 6.5 = 442 B, DSpark draft 36 B; one KV
#   head, so TP does not shard it): a 1M context is 1.89 GiB per rank. The
#   2026-10-19 logs show more (prefill 5.56 GiB for 1.5M tokens = 3.8 KB/token,
#   decode 8.10 GiB for 4M = 2.07 KB/token); the launcher's 10.5 MiB per SWA ring
#   (272 prefill, 128 decode) covers part of the gap.
#   Prefill, 1.5M pool: pool 5.63, free 13.12 after graphs, of which 10 is the
#   transient reserve for eager chunks (MoE buffers, indexer logits tiles of up to
#   2 GiB). The KV alone would fit ~3.2M tokens: the limit at 1M is eager-chunk
#   headroom, not KV. Measured at 262K with a 1M pool: 14.6 GB free after capture
#   with 8K chunks ran clean; 10.7 GB with 12K chunks OOMed (fragmentation).
#   This pool costs ~1.9 GiB of that (3.8 KB/token slope), leaving ~12.6 GB.
#   Decode, 6M pool: pool 12.67, free 14.07 (6 reserved). Not modelled: the
#   request tables, rows x (context + 16) x int32 for req_to_token and the Engram
#   n-gram token table: ~1.0 GiB on decode (130 rows), 0.13 GiB on prefill, 4x
#   their 262K size.
#   Concurrent 1M requests: prefill holds one in flight (plus 512K of others);
#   decode holds six. Prefill throughput sets the rate (~35K tok/s per pair
#   measured at 262K, so a cold 1M prompt is 30 s or more; sparse attention cost
#   grows with the prefix).
# GPU checks before this is qualified: "free after graph capture" in both
# workers' logs (prefill >= 12 GB, else drop the pool to 1048576), a cold 1M
# prompt alone and under realmix load with 0 NVRM errors, then 2097152 on
# prefill if the headroom holds.
DSV41_LAUNCH_ARGS=--gpu-models B200 --memory-profile B200 --context-length 1048576 --warmups confidential_cold_path --loader-threads 2 --chunk-size 8192 --prefill-requests 16 --prefill-schedule-policy hrrn --decode-requests 128 --decode-graph-extra-bs 10,12,14 --decode-polling-interval 2 --tokenizer-workers 4 --prefill-swa-prefix-tails 256 --max-total-tokens 1572864 --prefill-hicache-ratio auto --decode-max-total-tokens 6291456 --mem-fraction 0.92 --custom-all-reduce on --prefill-env SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_ENGRAM_STAGING_PREFETCH=1 --prefill-env SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_GATHER_THREADS=8 --prefill-env NCCL_PROTO=LL128 --prefill-env SGLANG_ENABLE_DISAGG_PREFILL_EARLY_RESULT=1 --prefill-env SGLANG_HRRN_SIZE_EXPONENT=1.5 --prefill-env SGLANG_OPT_PREFIX_PROMPT_ENCODE=1 --decode-env SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_ENGRAM_STAGING_PREFETCH=1 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_GATHER_THREADS=8 --decode-env SGLANG_OPT_PREFIX_PROMPT_ENCODE=1 --prefill-graph-max-seq-len 65536 --compact-host-memory --kernel-cache-dir /data/dsv41-bringup/container-cache/dsv41-pd-latest --decode-radix-cache --router-max-concurrent-requests 192 --router-queue-size 256 --router-queue-timeout-secs 30 --prefill-env SGLANG_DISAGGREGATION_WAITING_TIMEOUT=1200 --decode-env SGLANG_DISAGGREGATION_WAITING_TIMEOUT=1200
DSV41_EXTRA_ARGS=
